cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "Forecasting Observed Desert Locust Swarm Occurrence from Weather and Radar"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible hindcast pipeline testing whether Sentinel-1 radar and ERA5-Land
  reanalysis can forecast observed adult desert locust swarm occurrence as a proxy
  for potential settlement habitat, using the 2020
  East Africa outbreak. Trains on flightless hopper bands and tests on mobile adult
  swarms to prevent re-detection, benchmarks feature sets under a fixed model
  specification, and reports random, spatial-block and forward-temporal validation
  together. Finds that Sentinel-1 degrades performance and that a distance-to-known-
  infestation baseline using no satellite data outperforms the satellite model.
type: software
